e glass containing blue liquid with a green band marking the water level.\n","first_frame":"assets/234d5c8be03a67c99ec6.png","source_video":null,"candidates":[],"events":[{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-12T10:03:53.796326+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'ls -la; cat prompt.txt; cat GENERATION_RULES.md'","aggregated_output":"total 68\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 tiger tiger  4096 Nov 12 18:03 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 tiger tiger  4096 Nov 12 18:01 ..\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 12 18:03 .agents\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 12 18:03 .aws\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 12 18:03 .codex\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 12 18:03 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger  4096 Nov 12 18:01 .tmp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger  1093 Nov  9 23:58 GENERATION_RULES.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger  4026 Nov  6 02:01 artifact_io.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger 37308 Oct 30 19:21 first_frame.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger  3262 Nov  6 02:01 player_template.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger   527 Oct 30 19:21 prompt.txt\nStatic locked-off single-shot with fixed frame throughout filmed with constant framerate in real-time. The scene shows a realistic scientific demonstration. The scene only contains the described setup and actions. The blue-black grabber tool was holding the small crumpled piece of paper at the inner rim of the glass containing the blue liquid and the green water level marking. The blue-black grabber releases the small crumpled piece of paper into the glass containing blue liquid with a green band marking the water level.\n# PixelWorld generation contract v2\n\n- Use only `first_frame.png` and `prompt.txt`. Work inside this workspace. No network, other cases, reference continuations, masks, scores, memory, external AI models, learned weights, external simulation/rendering engines, or subagents.\n- Generate 20 RGB frames at 256×144, 4 fps, for 5 seconds. Frame 00 must be pixel-identical to `first_frame.png`.\n- You must create `generate.py`, run it, and call `artifact_io.save(frames, case_dir)` at least once before finishing. Finish only after the required output artifacts exist. Keep `generate.py` runnable so it regenerates the submitted RGB video.\n- Local Python drawing, image operations, shading, analytic geometry and mathematical dynamics are allowed.\n- Choose your own approach and use the tools permitted by your Track. If you revise the video, save each revised candidate before continuing. Avoid repeated revision without a clear expected improvement; aim for high-quality output while considering efficiency.\n- Use `.tmp/` for temporary files. No additional planning or method report is required.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-12T10:06:45.702452+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat artifact_io.py; echo \"----\"; cat player_template.html'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Output-only helpers. No drawing or generation policy is implemented here.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport base64\nimport json\nimport wave\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\ndef save(frames, case_dir, audio=None):\n    case_dir = Path(case_dir)\n    frames = np.asarray(frames)\n    path = case_dir / \"task_spec.json\"\n    spec = json.loads(path.read_text()) if path.is_file() else {}\n    n, h, w, fps = (spec.get(\"frames\", 20), spec.get(\"height\", 144), spec.get(\"width\", 256), spec.get(\"fps\", 4))\n    assert frames.shape == (n, h, w, 3) and frames.dtype == np.uint8, frames.shape\n    audio_spec = spec.get(\"audio\")\n    audio_url = None\n    if audio_spec:\n        samples = round(n / fps * audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n        pcm = np.asarray(audio)\n        if pcm.ndim == 1:\n            pcm = pcm[:, None]\n        assert pcm.shape == (samples, audio_spec[\"channels\"]) and pcm.dtype == np.int16, (pcm.shape, pcm.dtype)\n        with wave.open(str(case_dir / \"audio.wav\"), \"wb\") as handle:\n            handle.setnchannels(audio_spec[\"channels\"])\n            handle.setsampwidth(2)\n            handle.setframerate(audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n            handle.writeframes(pcm.astype(\"<i2\").tobytes())\n        audio_url = \"data:audio/wav;base64,\" + base64.b64encode((case_dir / \"audio.wav\").read_bytes()).decode()\n    values = frames.astype(np.uint32)\n    packed = (values[:, :, :, 0] << 16) | (values[:, :, :, 1] << 8) | values[:, :, :, 2]\n    tensor = packed.transpose(1, 2, 0)\n    np.savez_compressed(case_dir / \"pixels.npz\", pixels=tensor)\n\n    folder = case_dir / \"frames\"\n    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    for index, frame in enumerate(frames):\n        Image.fromarray(frame).save(folder / f\"{index:02d}.png\")\n\n    sheet = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, (h + 21) * 2), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(sheet)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(np.linspace(0, n - 1, 8).round().astype(int)):\n        x, y = (index % 4) * w, (index // 4) * (h + 21)\n        draw.text((x + 5, y + 3), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        sheet.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, y + 21))\n    sheet.save(case_dir / \"inspection.png\")\n\n    transition = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, h * 2 + 21), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(transition)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(min(i, n-1) for i in range(4)):\n        x = index * w\n        draw.text((x + 5, 4), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        transition.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, 21))\n        transition.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]).resize((w, h), Image.Resampling.NEAREST), (x, h + 21))\n    transition.save(case_dir / \"transition_check.png\")\n\n    encode = lambda array: base64.b64encode(np.asarray(array, dtype=\"<u4\").tobytes()).decode()\n    deltas = []\n    for index in range(1, n):\n        current = packed[index].reshape(-1)\n        previous = packed[index - 1].reshape(-1)\n        positions = np.flatnonzero(current != previous)\n        packet = []\n        if len(positions):\n            bounds = np.r_[0, np.flatnonzero(np.diff(positions) > 1) + 1, len(positions)]\n            for start, end in zip(bounds[:-1], bounds[1:]):\n                offset = int(positions[start])\n                count = int(end - start)\n                packet.extend([offset, count])\n                packet.extend(current[offset:offset + count].tolist())\n        deltas.append(encode(packet))\n    data = {\n        \"id\": case_dir.name,\n        \"width\": w, \"height\": h, \"frames\": n, \"fps\": fps, \"audio\": audio_url,\n        \"first\": encode(packed[0].reshape(-1)),\n        \"deltas\": deltas,\n        \"caption\": (case_dir / \"prompt.txt\").read_text().strip(),\n    }\n    template = (Path(__file__).parent / \"player_template.html\").read_text()\n    payload = json.dumps(data, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\")\n    (case_dir / \"index.html\").write_text(template.replace(\"__ID__\", case_dir.name).replace(\"__DATA__\", payload))\n----\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PixelWorld · __ID__</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:16px;background:#101419;color:#eef3f7;font:14px system-ui,sans-serif}canvas{display:block;width:min(100%,768px);height:auto;image-rendering:pixelated;background:#080a0c;border-radius:8px;margin:auto}.controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;max-width:768px;margin:14px auto 0}button{background:#a5ef83;border:0;border-radius:7px;color:#142110;padding:9px 16px;font:inherit;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}input[type=range]{flex:1;min-width:100px}.caption{max-width:768px;margin:12px auto;color:#a7b0be;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}</style>\n<canvas id=\"canvas\" width=\"256\" height=\"144\"></canvas><div class=\"controls\"><button id=\"play\">Play</button><button id=\"replay\">Replay</button><input id=\"seek\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"19\" value=\"0\"><output id=\"time\"></output><label><input id=\"loop\" type=\"checkbox\" checked> Loop</label></div><div id=\"caption\" class=\"caption\"></div>\n<script>'use strict';const DATA=__DATA__,W=DATA.width||256,H=DATA.height||144,N=DATA.frames||20,FPS=DATA.fps||4;function unpack(s){const t=atob(s),b=new Uint8Array(t.length);for(let i=0;i<t.length;i++)b[i]=t.charCodeAt(i);return new Uint32Array(b.buffer)}const frames=[unpack(DATA.first)];for(const encoded of DATA.deltas){const f=new Uint32Array(frames.at(-1)),p=unpack(encoded);for(let i=0;i<p.length;){const start=p[i++],count=p[i++];f.set(p.subarray(i,i+count),start);i+=count}frames.push(f)}const canvas=document.getElementById('canvas'),ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');canvas.width=W;canvas.height=H;const img=ctx.createImageData(W,H);seek.max=N-1;const audio=DATA.audio?new Audio(DATA.audio):null;let frame=0,playing=false,raf=null,started=0;function draw(n){frame=Math.max(0,Math.min(N-1,n));const pixels=frames[frame];for(let i=0;i<pixels.length;i++){const v=pixels[i],p=i*4;img.data[p]=v>>>16;img.data[p+1]=(v>>>8)&255;img.data[p+2]=v&255;img.data[p+3]=255}ctx.putImageData(img,0,0);seek.value=frame;time.textContent=`${frame+1}/${N} · ${(frame/FPS).toFixed(2)} / ${(N/FPS).toFixed(2)}s`}function pause(){playing=false;cancelAnimationFrame(raf);if(audio)audio.pause();play.textContent='Play'}function tick(t){if(!playing)return;let elapsed=audio?audio.currentTime:(t-started)/1000;if(elapsed>=N/FPS){if(loop.checked){started=t;if(audio){audio.currentTime=0;audio.play()}elapsed=0}else{draw(N-1);pause();return}}draw(Math.min(N-1,Math.floor(elapsed*FPS)));raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}async function start(){if(playing)return;if(frame===N-1)draw(0);started=performance.now()-frame/FPS*1000;if(audio){audio.currentTime=frame/FPS;try{await audio.play()}catch(e){caption.textContent='Audio playback failed: '+e.message;return}}playing=true;play.textContent='Pause';raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}play.onclick=()=>playing?pause():start();replay.onclick=()=>{pause();draw(0);start()};seek.oninput=e=>{pause();draw(+e.target.value)};caption.textContent=DATA.caption+(audio?' · RGB + PCM audio':'');if(audio)audio.onended=()=>{if(playing&&loop.checked){audio.currentTime=0;audio.play()}else pause()};draw(0);window.__pixelReady=true;</script></html>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-12T10:06:45.945533+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c \\\"from PIL import Image; im=Image.open('first_frame.png'); print(im.size, im.mode)\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"(256, 144) RGB\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"agent_message","utc":"2026-11-12T10:09:23.487630+00:00","text":"Let me examine the first frame closely, especially the top region where the grabber and paper should be.\n"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-12T10:09:24.679582+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd .tmp && python3 -c \\\"\nfrom PIL import Image\nim=Image.open('../first_frame.png')\n# crop top region and upscale\ntop=im.crop((80,0,180,60)).resize((400,240), Image.Resampling.NEAREST)\ntop.save('top_zoom.png')\nfull=im.resize((1024,576), Image.Resampling.NEAREST)\nfull.save('full_zoom.png')\nprint('ok')\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"ok\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-12T10:17:30.120849+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd .tmp && python3 -c \\\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\nim=np.array(Image.open('../first_frame.png'))\nH,W,_=im.shape\nprint('shape',im.shape)\n# find strongly blue pixels (grabber): B high, R low\nr,g,b=im[...,0].astype(int),im[...,1].astype(int),im[...,2].astype(int)\nmask=(b>90)&(b-r>40)&(b-g>20)\nys,xs=np.where(mask)\nprint('blue count',len(xs))\nif len(xs):\n  print('bbox x',xs.min(),xs.max(),'y',ys.min(),ys.max())\n# cluster by x columns\nimport collections\ncols=collections.Counter(xs.tolist())\nprint('blue cols sorted:', sorted(cols.items(